    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Initial package 0.37.0: core CLI built with maturin (pyo3
headroom._core)
* Requires distro ast-grep rather than the ast-grep-cli PyPI
  wheel; binaries.resolve() searches PATH
* ExclusiveArch rust_tier1_arches; crates vendored with
  cargo_vendor mode=manual
* headroom-proxy subpackage is headroom-ai[proxy]: FastAPI,
  uvicorn, magika, onnxruntime, sqlite-vec, and the rest of
  the CLI gate (ensure_proxy_dependencies)
* headroom-proxy is noarch (Requires-only extra)

INTERDEPENDENT REQUESTS - please stage together (will not build until these land):
 * sr#1376401 - python-magika (headroom-proxy runtime)
 * sr#1376402 - python-sqlite-vec (headroom-proxy --memory)</comment>
    <requestid>1376404</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>4e9dab01eaa938b0e55a999197bb023d</srcmd5>
    <version>0.38.0</version>
    <time>1790101827</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.38.0.

Two proxy denial-of-service fixes ship in this release: the existing
bound on decompressed request bodies, and a new 64 KiB cap on the
/admin/runtime-env request body that does not trust the client's
Content-Length. Upstream marks the latter a security fix; no CVE was
assigned.

The vendored rustls moves to 0.23.45 for RUSTSEC-2026-0285, which is
real for this package: rustls is in the shipped cdylib graph via
ureq, and the advisory lists 0.23.45 as the patched version.

New commands: headroom-cache-ttl (offline cache-TTL estimator) and
headroom telemetry.

Worth flagging for review: this package's telemetry beacon is opt-out
and on by default, and 0.38.0 widens its payload. That is unchanged
in kind from 0.37.0, which is already in Factory, and the new
&quot;headroom telemetry&quot; command exists precisely to show what is sent.
The gzip transport added upstream ships disabled, so it is not
claimed in the changelog.

litellm is raised to &gt;= 1.96.2, following upstream, and is no longer
conditional on the Python version; Factory has 1.101.0.

Built and checked locally on aarch64: 27 tests pass, rpmlint 0
errors and 0 badness. The single warning is the pre-existing,
deliberate python-missing-require for ast-grep-cli, since the spec
uses the distribution's ast-grep binary instead of the PyPI wheel.</comment>
    <requestid>1379700</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>ff3bdc3fc04a8e650583e6e52ce54cc8</srcmd5>
    <version>0.39.0</version>
    <time>1790585163</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update headroom to 0.39.0.

Only Version: moved in the spec - upstream's core dependencies and the
whole [proxy] extra are byte-identical to 0.38.0, so every Requires and
BuildRequires floor was re-verified rather than changed.

The vendored crates were refreshed with the package's existing
cargo_vendor service (mode=manual, update=true, which is why fancy-regex
moved 0.17.0 -&gt; 0.19.2 and lazy_static was dropped within their semver
ranges, independent of the lockfile). The licence set was re-derived
from the new tree rather than inherited: still Apache-2.0 AND MPL-2.0,
option-ext 0.2.0 the only copyleft. The Legal-Review-Notice counts are
refreshed to 276/535.

0.39.0's two commits labelled &quot;security:&quot; are deliberately not credited
as security fixes. The Copilot OAuth one is real and shipped: the token
is written to a private temp file and renamed into place, so a refused
chmod can no longer leave the refresh token world-readable. &quot;Reject
unauthenticated public proxy binds&quot; is a 0.0.0.0 -&gt; 127.0.0.1 change in
Dockerfile and install.sh with no shipped file touched, and
proxy/server.py already refused it at 0.38.0.

Native aarch64 build green, %check 27 passed, rpmlint 0 errors /
0 badness (2 pre-existing warnings: the ast-grep substitution and the
inherent unstripped extension module).

No CVE is named in the crossed range and no Bugzilla report references
this package.
</comment>
    <requestid>1380833</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="4" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>76f865ddd9aca090fdf7dede4e6cefca</srcmd5>
    <version>0.39.1</version>
    <time>1790696986</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.39.1, which makes the proxy token-per-minute limiter opt-in again so a stock proxy is no longer a 100k tokens/minute throttle, and stops large-context requests from getting a 429 they can never satisfy; crates/ and Cargo.lock are byte-identical to 0.39.0, so the vendored tree and licence set are unchanged.

Built green on aarch64 (rpmlint 0 errors, %check 27 passed) against openSUSE:Tumbleweed, because a Factory:ARM build is currently impossible for a reason unrelated to this package: the published python313-httpx2 there is still 2.12.0-1.1 with an exact httpcore2 version pin, while only 2.13.1-1.1 exists. Details in .changes.
</comment>
    <requestid>1381240</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
